# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/

# Env files. The bare ".env" pattern alone only matches a file literally named that — it
# does NOT match "service/.env.whale-alert-connector" (a real secrets file, not an example
# template), which is exactly the gap ".env.*" plus the "!...example" exceptions close.
# Two example-exception shapes are needed: "!.env.*.example" for a named variant like
# "service/.env.whale-alert-connector.example", and "!.env.example" for the plain form
# used elsewhere in this repo (the root and service/ own templates) — the "*" in the first
# pattern requires a non-empty middle segment, so it doesn't also cover the second, plain
# shape (confirmed the hard way: a freshly added "peer-service/.env.example" was silently
# swallowed by ".env.*" until this line was added; the two pre-existing plain ones only
# survived because they were already tracked before ".env.*" existed at all).
.env
.env.*
!.env.*.example
!.env.example
client-mqtt/config.js
client-long-poll/config.js
client-admin/config.js
client-ws/config.js
docker-compose.override.yml

# TLS certs generated locally by scripts/setup-tls.sh (.ps1) — per-machine, never committed
certs/

